Z||000000||Formula||07-23-99||09:35 AM||||Heres the story, I was sitting at a red stop light next to a dark green neon, and he reved up his puny motor. I did the same. I put my blaze red fiero back into drive and pushed on the small black gas pedal. All of a sudden grey smoke started pouring from the back of my beautiful car, it was also making an extremely loud squeling noise. What could have happened?  So I shuffeled over to the bank of the road and thoroughly investigated. My brand new tires were a firey reddish orange, and the fiberglass rear end of my little hot rod was covered in a blackish rubber substance.  I figured that I best be getting to the troublesome pontiac dealership. As I get on the all-mighty freeway I decide to push my awesome v6 to the max. All I heard was a LOUD boom of the sonic nature, I turned on my black CB radio and listened to channel 1. A place called USAF(?) had reported a low flying russian aircraft (RED) going at MACH 5. After listening to the cumbersome report I approached my small exit ramp to the metropolis of Fieroville.  I whizzed by the giant sign of ed parks and continued to the pontiac dealership.  I pulled into the Fiero lot and asked a technician what happened. He said "WOW."  Sorry about the story but I couldn't help it. 
